<Site title="Corrections and contributions" description="Help improve the accuracy and source quality of the Demonology archive.">
<section class="wrap archive methodology"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH INTEGRITY</p><h1>Corrections and contributions</h1><p class="lead">The archive develops through careful source examination and transparent correction. We welcome specific, constructive submissions that strengthen its accuracy.</p><h2>What to include</h2><ul><li>The article ID or page URL.</li><li>The passage, historical claim, translation, citation or image attribution that needs attention.</li><li>A proposed correction and an identifiable supporting source, with a precise locator where available.</li></ul><h2>Submit a correction</h2><p>Use the public project issue tracker to report a source error, missing reference, accessibility problem or other improvement. Submissions may be visible publicly. Do not include personal information, private correspondence, medical histories or allegations about identifiable people.</p><p><a class="primary" href="https://github.com/andrewzaia/Demonology/issues/new?title=Research%20correction">Submit a correction</a></p><p><a href="https://github.com/andrewzaia/Demonology/issues">Browse existing submissions</a></p><h2>How corrections are handled</h2><p>Corrections are evaluated against the cited source and the archive's evidence methodology. Material revisions preserve stable identifiers and are documented in the public change history. Approval to publish is not a guarantee that every interpretation is beyond revision.</p><p><a href="/methodology/">Read the research methodology</a> · <a href="/about/">About the archive</a></p></section>
</Site>
